import { BytesReaderCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> BytesReaderCopy = BytesReaderCopy {
  summary: "ByteError describes an integer outside 0 through 255. With fromInts, ByteOutOfRange lets you read the first value that did not fit.",
  taskTitle: "Explain which input cannot fit in a byte",
  purpose: "Build a small binary payload from a numeric array. Every byte must be from 0 through 255. If a value is outside that range, report it so the original input can be corrected.",
  typescriptBefore: "Uint8Array.from converts out-of-range numbers too, so TypeScript first checks Number.isInteger and the range. find returns the first invalid value. If every value is valid, the example creates a Uint8Array and displays its elements as an array.",
  benefit: "TypeScript can perform the same validation. Seseragi’s fromInts includes a ByteError in its return value on failure. Separate branches handle the successful Bytes and the integer that explains the rejected input.",
  setup: "import * as bytes defines an alias for std/bytes. fn defines describe. values: Array<Int> declares an integer-array parameter; -> String declares the returned string. bytes.fromInts values is a call passing values to that function.",
  after: [
    "Either<ByteError, Bytes> means one of two outcomes: Left containing a failure, or Right containing the successful Bytes. match selects that branch and returns the expression after its ->.",
    "Left (bytes.ByteOutOfRange value) reads the error inside Left as ByteOutOfRange and names the offending integer value. The backtick string inserts that integer into the message at ${value}.",
    "Right content names the successful Bytes. bytes.toInts content copies it to an integer array; show turns the array into a display String. The parentheses in show (bytes.toInts content) pass the inner call’s result to show.",
    "For [1, 256, -1], 256 is found first, so the message is only Out of range: 256. [-1] reports -1. An empty input succeeds with empty Bytes and displays [].",
  ],
  details: [
    "ByteOutOfRange carries the invalid integer itself, not its array position or a list of every problem. fromInts checks in source order and stops at the first invalid value. It returns no partially successful Bytes.",
    "ByteError keeps its representation private, but the public ByteOutOfRange form shown here lets you read its content. You do not need to parse an error-message string to recover the number.",
    "The operation does not wrap 256 to 0 or treat -1 as 255. Correct the input to the intended integer from 0 through 255 before converting again. An array of Float values is not Array<Int> either, so it cannot be passed directly to fromInts.",
  ],
  nodeNote: "The find, Number.isInteger, Uint8Array.from, and Array.from operations in this TypeScript example are also available on Node 24.19.0. It uses none of Bun’s hexadecimal or Base64 helpers.",
}
